    {
      "directNodeIds": [
        "math:defined-binary-operation-evaluation"
      ],
      "explanation": "The rule cubes the first input and squares the second, so the order of the inputs matters. Applying it to each ordered pair gives\n\\[\n2\\heartsuit4=2^3\\cdot4^2=8\\cdot16=128\n\\]\nand\n\\[\n4\\heartsuit2=4^3\\cdot2^2=64\\cdot4=256.\n\\]\nThe denominator is nonzero, so\n\\[\n\\frac{2\\heartsuit4}{4\\heartsuit2}\n=\\frac{128}{256}=\\frac12.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(\\tfrac12\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{B}\\).",
      "id": "apply-definition",
      "sourceRef": "amc/2016_AMC_10B_Q02#apply-definition",
      "title": "Apply the operation rule"
    }
  ],
